{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Breeze feels like a natural next choice after Old Sock because I want more of Clapton's relaxed blues playing and song-focused music.",
    "Standing in the Breach appeals to the thoughtful songwriting and roots-oriented sound I enjoyed in You Should Be So Lucky; Croz and Cass County also fit parts of that interest."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Houses of the Holy and Physical Graffiti lean toward heavier rock than I want today; my interest in Hendrix does not mean that heaviness is what I am seeking.",
    "Wings Over America and Live at the Academy of Music are less immediate choices because I prefer a studio record today, while The Endless River offers less of the vocal storytelling I want."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to treat an interest in established rock musicians as a broad interest in their peers, even when the sound and songwriting feel quite different.",
    "My interest in guitar playing seems to have been stretched into an interest in heavier or atmospheric rock, although relaxed blues songs are more appealing right now."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The connection from Old Sock to relaxed blues and JJ Cale's songs matters more to me than a general classic-rock connection.",
    "I am selective about what I choose now: familiar musicians, thoughtful vocals, and a studio album give me stronger reasons to listen than a broadly promising roots-rock sound."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in roots-oriented music but extend it too broadly beyond the relaxed blues and thoughtful, vocal-led studio records I want today."
}"}
